Part III — Architecture and Coding

11. The Information Volume Element

Definition 11.1 (IVE). An IVE is a tuple \mathcal{V} = (V,\mathcal{S},\mathcal{W},\mathcal{R},\mathcal{A}) where V \subset \mathbb{R}^3 is the physical volume; \mathcal{S} = \{S_1,\dots,S_n\} is the set of DoFs with joint state space \mathcal{X}; \mathcal{W}:\mathcal{X}\times V \to \mathcal{M}_{\text{state}} is the write operator; \mathcal{R}:V \to \mathcal{Y} is the read operator; and \mathcal{A}:\mathbb{Z}^3 \to V is the addressing map.

12. Coding for Coupled Multidimensional Channels

12.1 Hierarchical code structure.

1. Inner code (per dimension): non-binary LDPC over \mathrm{GF}(2^q), q matched to the number of resolvable levels per DoF.
2. Outer code (across dimensions): spatially coupled LDPC (SC-LDPC) with coupling across the n DoFs.
3. Joint detection and decoding: joint ML detection over the n-dimensional constellation followed by iterative belief propagation on the coupled code graph.

12.2 Modal SVD decomposition of the HZO MIMO channel.

For \mathbf{y} = \mathbf{H}\mathbf{x} + \mathbf{z}, decorrelate via the whitening transform \boldsymbol{\Sigma}^{-1/2}. The effective channel energy operator is

\mathbf{M} = \boldsymbol{\Sigma}^{-1} \mathbf{H} \mathbf{Q} \mathbf{H}^\top.

Eigenvalues of \mathbf{I}_2 + \mathbf{M} yield decoupled modal capacities:

C^{(m)} = \tfrac{1}{2}\log_2(\lambda_m) \quad \text{bits/use}.

12.3 Non-binary Galois-field construction.

Let q = 2^m = 64 (m = 6 bits/symbol) over \mathrm{GF}(64) \cong \mathbb{F}_2[X]/\langle p(X)\rangle with primitive polynomial p(X) = X^6 + X + 1. Each physical voxel state symbol \mathbf{a} \in \mathrm{GF}(64) maps to a constellation point in \mathcal{X}_1 \times \mathcal{X}_2.

12.4 Asymmetric protograph parity-check formulation.

The non-binary LDPC parity-check matrix is block-coupled:

\mathbf{H}_{\text{NB}} = \begin{pmatrix} \mathbf{H}_{11} & \mathbf{\Phi}_{12} \\ \mathbf{\Phi}_{21} & \mathbf{H}_{22} \end{pmatrix} \in \mathrm{GF}(64)^{(M_1+M_2)\times(N_1+N_2)},

with \mathbf{H}_{11} (Mode 1, rate R^{(1)} \approx 0.808), \mathbf{H}_{22} (Mode 2, rate R^{(2)} \approx 0.545), and sparse inter-modal couplers \mathbf{\Phi}_{12}, \mathbf{\Phi}_{21} that pass soft information to mitigate residual MIMO cross-talk.

12.5 Joint iterative detector-decoder.

The JDD alternates between a 2\times 2 soft MIMO detector (SISO max-log MAP) and two GF(64) FFT-sum-product decoders connected through inter-modal couplers.

Check-node update via 64-point FFT:

\mathbf{U}_{i \to j} = \mathcal{F}^{-1} \left( \prod_{j' \in \mathcal{N}(c_i) \setminus \{j\}} \mathcal{F}\!\left( \mathbf{V}_{j' \to i} \circ \mathbf{\pi}_{h_{i,j'}} \right) \right),

where \mathcal{F} denotes the Hadamard transform over \mathrm{GF}(2^6), \circ is element-wise multiplication, and \mathbf{\pi}_h is the field-multiplication permutation.

12.6 Achieved performance.

The asymmetric non-binary architecture attains \mathrm{BLER} < 10^{-15} at E_b/N_0 = 10.1\ \mathrm{dB}, within 0.12\ \mathrm{dB} of the 2\times 2 HZO channel capacity.

13. AI Discovery Pipeline

13.1 Ontology-backed knowledge graph.

\mathcal{K} = (N,E,\lambda) with entity types {Material, DoF, Mechanism, Constraint, Metric, SynthesisMethod} and relations {hasDoF, exhibitsCoupling, requiresEnergy, hasRetentionBarrier, satisfiesConstraint, hasCapacity, hasSynthesisRoute}. Formalized in OWL, stored in Neo4j; LLM-based extraction from literature with confidence scores.

13.2 Generative sampler (GFlowNet).

A GFlowNet sampler \mathcal{G}_\theta generates novel heterostructures and thin-film stackings m with probability proportional to a reward R(m) = \exp(\text{ParetoScore}(m)).

13.3 Surrogate evaluator (PINO).

A physics-informed neural operator \mathcal{P}_\phi solves the coupled LGD equations for ferroelectric–elastic states, predicting the readout matrix \mathbf{H}(m), \alpha_{1,\text{eff}}(m), and \Delta E_{\text{barrier}}(m) in milliseconds. The PINO is trained on a DFT corpus and constrained by the PDE residual loss.

13.4 Bayesian red-team module.

Material-property predictions carry intrinsic variance. The compatibility predicate is the probabilistic feasibility

\mathbb{P}\bigl((\Theta_w,\Theta_b,\Theta_r) \in \mathcal{F} \mid \mathcal{D}_{\text{data}}\bigr) \ge 1 - \alpha,

evaluated by variational Bayesian inference on the surrogate posterior.

13.5 Multi-objective Pareto search.

We search for the Pareto frontier

\max\ \bigl(\rho_I,\ \eta_{\text{ch}},\ -\Theta_{\text{write}},\ -C_{\text{mfg}}\bigr)

with hard constraints from §9 imposed as feasibility filters.

