14. Material System and Channel Parameters

Voxel side d = 10\ \mathrm{nm} (baseline) and d = 6.5\ \mathrm{nm} (scaled). DoFs: S_1 = P_z (remanent polarization P_r \approx 0.20\ \mathrm{C}/\mathrm{m}^2); S_2 = \epsilon_{zz} (recoverable strain \epsilon_{\max} \approx 0.005).

Constitutive relations:

\begin{pmatrix} D_z \\ \sigma_{zz} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \epsilon_{33}^T & e_{33} \\ -e_{33} & c_{33}^E \end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix} E_z \\ \epsilon_{zz} \end{pmatrix},

with e_{33} \approx 1.8\ \mathrm{C}/\mathrm{m}^2, c_{33}^E \approx 2.2\times 10^{11}\ \mathrm{N}/\mathrm{m}^2, \epsilon_{33}^T \approx 2.5\times 10^{-10}\ \mathrm{F}/\mathrm{m}.

Normalized states x_1 = P_z/P_r, x_2 = \epsilon_{zz}/\epsilon_{\max}. Readout channel:

\mathbf{H} = \begin{pmatrix}1.00 & 0.25\\ 0.35 & 1.00\end{pmatrix},\quad \boldsymbol{\Sigma} = \begin{pmatrix}0.0400 & 0.0120\\ 0.0120 & 0.0900\end{pmatrix},\quad \mathbf{Q} = \mathbf{I}_2,\ P = 2.

Here h_{21} = 0.35 is strain induced by polarization reversal (converse piezoelectric); h_{12} = 0.25 is polarization charge induced by mechanical stress (direct piezoelectric). Noise: charge-integrator \sigma_1^2 = 0.040, interferometric strain \sigma_2^2 = 0.090, cross-correlated substrate vibration \rho = 0.20.

15. MIMO Capacity and Coupling Penalty

\det\boldsymbol{\Sigma} = 0.003456,

\boldsymbol{\Sigma}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix}26.0417 & -3.4722 \\ -3.4722 & 11.5741\end{pmatrix},

\mathbf{H}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{H}^\top = \begin{pmatrix}1.0625 & 0.6000\\ 0.6000 & 1.1225\end{pmatrix},\quad \mathbf{M} = \boldsymbol{\Sigma}^{-1}\mathbf{H}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{H}^\top = \begin{pmatrix}25.5860 & 11.7275\\ 3.2553 & 10.9086\end{pmatrix}.

Joint capacity:

\det(\mathbf{I}_2+\mathbf{M}) = 278.4256,\quad C_n = \tfrac{1}{2}\log_2(278.4256) = 4.0605\ \text{bits/read/voxel}.

Corrected product-restricted sum-rate. With independent Gaussian inputs and diagonal \mathbf{Q} = \operatorname{diag}(q_1,q_2), the mutual informations in the same joint channel are

I(X_i;Y_i) = \frac{1}{2}\log_2\!\left(1 + \frac{H_{ii}^2\,q_i}{\sigma_i^2 + \sum_{j\neq i} H_{ij}^2\,q_j}\right).

For the equal-power allocation q_1 = q_2 = 1:

I_1 = \tfrac{1}{2}\log_2\!\left(1 + \frac{1}{0.04 + 0.0625}\right) = \tfrac{1}{2}\log_2(10.756) = 1.7120,

I_2 = \tfrac{1}{2}\log_2\!\left(1 + \frac{1}{0.09 + 0.1225}\right) = \tfrac{1}{2}\log_2(5.706) = 1.2547.

Sum: 2.9667. Optimizing over q_1+q_2 = 2 yields a marginal improvement to C_2^{\perp} \approx 2.97.

Coupling penalty and operational independence coefficient:

\Delta C = C_2^{\perp} - C_n = 2.97 - 4.0605 = -1.09\ \text{bits/read/voxel},

\eta_{\text{ch}} = \frac{C_n}{C_2^{\perp}} = \frac{4.0605}{2.97} \approx 1.37.

Interpretation. The HZO channel is strongly constructive: the off-diagonal cross-talk is more than compensated by the joint-detection gain of the 2\times 2 MIMO architecture. The HZO matrix has |\mathbf{H}| = 0.9375 and is well-conditioned with \kappa(\mathbf{H}) \approx 1.9.

16. Volumetric Information Density

