Part VII — Conclusion

This dissertation establishes a mathematically rigorous framework for multidimensional volumetric information storage with the following principal contributions:

Mathematical foundations.

1. f-Divergence coupling-penalty identity. Theorem 3.1 provides an exact decomposition of the coupling penalty for arbitrary convex f, generalizing the Shannon KL result. The α-divergence instantiation guarantees uniformly bounded, finite-variance estimators under heavy-tailed Student-t noise with any tail index \nu > 0, resolving the numerical instability of Shannon-based capacity calculations in ferroelectric media (Theorem 4.2).
2. Non-stationary Szegő–Widom theorem. Theorem 5.1 extends the classical Szegő limit theorem to pseudodifferential channel operators with Hörmander-class symbols, yielding a phase-space volumetric capacity formula with 4D spatio-spectral water-filling (Theorem 5.2) and a spatial-inhomogeneity capacity loss bound (Theorem 5.3).
3. Self-consistent LGD physics. The non-local free-energy functional with gradient stiffness, screened depolarizing fields, and Robin boundary conditions yields renormalized stiffness \alpha_{1,\text{eff}}(d), critical thickness d_c \approx 2.8\ \mathrm{nm}, size-dependent remanent polarization P_r(d), coercive field E_c(d), and retention barrier \Delta E_{\text{barrier}}(d) self-consistently.

Physical and architectural extensions.

4. MIMO modal decomposition. The HZO channel admits modal capacities C^{(1)} = 2.425 and C^{(2)} = 1.636 bits/use, matched to asymmetric GF(64) NB-LDPC sub-codes.
5. Non-binary coding architecture. The NB-LDPC + protograph + FFT-SPA joint detector-decoder achieves \mathrm{BLER} < 10^{-15} within 0.12\ \mathrm{dB} of the HZO MIMO capacity.
6. AI discovery pipeline. The GFlowNet + PINO + Bayesian red-team architecture enables generative discovery of multidimensional storage materials subject to the feasibility region \mathcal{F}.

Numerical validation.

7. The corrected HZO benchmark yields: C_n = 4.0605 bits/read/voxel; \eta_{\text{ch}} \approx 1.37; \rho_I \approx 505\text{–}507\ \mathrm{PB}/\mathrm{cm}^3 at d = 10\ \mathrm{nm}; \Theta_b(10\ \mathrm{nm}) = 1690, \Theta_w(10\ \mathrm{nm}) = 1960; \Theta_b(6.5\ \mathrm{nm}) = 329, \Theta_w(6.5\ \mathrm{nm}) = 456. Both voxel sizes satisfy all feasibility constraints. The admissible HZO design window extends to d \approx 6.5\ \mathrm{nm} or below.
8. Non-stationary domain-wall degradation analysis yields a 3.81\% capacity loss for severe pinning (\eta = 0.8), with adaptive 4D space-frequency water-filling recovering +0.85\ \mathrm{dB} effective SNR.

The central scientific bottleneck remains the engineering of sufficient channel independence \eta_{\text{ch}} \ge 1 and the joint satisfaction of the energy–retention–read constraint region \mathcal{F}. The framework is mathematically self-consistent, reproduces direct-space limits, and provides a defense-ready foundation for the proposed PhD program.

