Appendix D — MIMO Channel Matrix Computations

D.1 HZO Constitutive Relations

\begin{pmatrix} D_z \\ \sigma_{zz} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \epsilon_{33}^T & e_{33} \\ -e_{33} & c_{33}^E \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} E_z \\ \epsilon_{zz} \end{pmatrix}.

Parameters: e_{33} = 1.8 C/m², c_{33}^E = 2.2 \times 10^{11} N/m², \epsilon_{33}^T = 2.5 \times 10^{-10} F/m.

Normalized states: x_1 = P_z/P_r, x_2 = \epsilon_{zz}/\epsilon_{\max} with P_r = 0.20 C/m², \epsilon_{\max} = 0.005.

Readout channel:

\mathbf{H} = \begin{pmatrix} 1.00 & 0.25 \\ 0.35 & 1.00 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \boldsymbol{\Sigma} = \begin{pmatrix} 0.0400 & 0.0120 \\ 0.0120 & 0.0900 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{Q} = \mathbf{I}_2, \quad P = 2.

D.2 Joint Capacity Computation

\det \boldsymbol{\Sigma} = 0.0400 \times 0.0900 - 0.0120^2 = 0.003600 - 0.000144 = 0.003456.

\boldsymbol{\Sigma}^{-1} = \frac{1}{0.003456} \begin{pmatrix} 0.0900 & -0.0120 \\ -0.0120 & 0.0400 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 26.0417 & -3.4722 \\ -3.4722 & 11.5741 \end{pmatrix}.

\mathbf{H}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{H}^\top = \begin{pmatrix} 1.00 & 0.25 \\ 0.35 & 1.00 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1.00 & 0.35 \\ 0.25 & 1.00 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0.6000 \\ 0.6000 & 1.1225 \end{pmatrix}.

\mathbf{M} = \boldsymbol{\Sigma}^{-1} \mathbf{H}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{H}^\top = \begin{pmatrix} 26.0417 & -3.4722 \\ -3.4722 & 11.5741 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0.6000 \\ 0.6000 & 1.1225 \end{pmatrix}.

Computing entry by entry:

M_{11} = 26.0417 \times 1.0625 + (-3.4722) \times 0.6000 = 27.669 - 2.083 = 25.586.

M_{12} = 26.0417 \times 0.6000 + (-3.4722) \times 1.1225 = 15.625 - 3.898 = 11.727.

M_{21} = -3.4722 \times 1.0625 + 11.5741 \times 0.6000 = -3.689 + 6.944 = 3.255.

M_{22} = -3.4722 \times 0.6000 + 11.5741 \times 1.1225 = -2.083 + 12.992 = 10.909.

\det(\mathbf{I}_2 + \mathbf{M}) = (1 + 25.586)(1 + 10.909) - 11.727 \times 3.255 = 26.586 \times 11.909 - 38.17 = 316.6 - 38.17 = 278.4.

C_n = \frac{1}{2} \log_2(278.4) = \frac{1}{2} \times 8.121 = 4.0605 bits/read/voxel.

D.3 Product-Restricted Sum-Rate

For independent inputs with \mathbf{Q} = \operatorname{diag}(q_1, q_2):

I(X_i; Y_i) = \frac{1}{2} \log_2\left( 1 + \frac{H_{ii}^2 q_i}{\sigma_i^2 + \sum_{j \neq i} H_{ij}^2 q_j} \right).

For q_1 = q_2 = 1:

I_1 = \frac{1}{2} \log_2\left( 1 + \frac{1}{0.04 + 0.0625} \right) = \frac{1}{2} \log_2(10.756) = 1.712.

I_2 = \frac{1}{2} \log_2\left( 1 + \frac{1}{0.09 + 0.1225} \right) = \frac{1}{2} \log_2(5.706) = 1.255.

Sum: C_2^{\perp} = 2.967.

Optimizing over q_1 + q_2 = 2 gives C_2^{\perp} \approx 2.97.

\eta_{\text{ch}} = \frac{4.0605}{2.97} = 1.37.

D.4 Modal Decomposition

The eigenvalues of \mathbf{I}_2 + \mathbf{M} are found from

\det(\mathbf{I}_2 + \mathbf{M} - \lambda \mathbf{I}) = 0.

\operatorname{tr}(\mathbf{I}_2 + \mathbf{M}) = 26.586 + 11.909 = 38.495.

\det(\mathbf{I}_2 + \mathbf{M}) = 278.4.

\lambda_{1,2} = \frac{38.495 \pm \sqrt{38.495^2 - 4 \times 278.4}}{2} = \frac{38.495 \pm \sqrt{1481.9 - 1113.6}}{2} = \frac{38.495 \pm 19.19}{2}.

\lambda_1 = 28.84, \quad \lambda_2 = 9.65.

C^{(1)} = \frac{1}{2} \log_2(28.84) = 2.425 bits/use.

C^{(2)} = \frac{1}{2} \log_2(9.65) = 1.636 bits/use.

